---
// Pure-noise factors: the chance that at least one of N tried factors passes a t-statistic bar by luck.
// Python (zoo.py, normal approx, two-sided): p(|t|>2)=0.0455, p(|t|>3)=0.0027; P(at least one) = 1-(1-p)^N.
// Monte Carlo (360 months, 400 trials) agreed: N=100 -> P(any |t|>3) 0.235 vs 0.237; N=400 -> 0.660 vs 0.661.
const N = [1, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 400];
const P2 = [0.046, 0.208, 0.372, 0.606, 0.903, 0.991, 1.0, 1.0];
const P3 = [0.003, 0.013, 0.027, 0.053, 0.126, 0.237, 0.418, 0.661];
const L = 80, R = 840, T = 60, B = 300;
const x = (n: number) => L + Math.log(n) / Math.log(400) * (R - L);
const y = (p: number) => B - p * (B - T);
const path = (P: number[]) => N.map((n, i) => `${i ? 'L' : 'M'}${x(n).toFixed(1)} ${y(P[i]).toFixed(1)}`).join(' ');
---
<figure class="p06f">
  <div class="p06f-scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 900 350" role="img" aria-label="Chance that at least one of N pure-noise factors looks significant by luck. With the bar at t above 2, it is 21 percent for 5 factors, 60 percent for 20, 90 percent for 50 and 99 percent for 100. With the bar at t above 3, it is 5 percent for 20, 24 percent for 100 and 66 percent for 400.">
      <text x="20" y="26" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>Try enough factors and one will look real</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Thử đủ nhiều factor thì thế nào cũng có một cái trông như thật</tspan></text>
      {[0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1].map((p) => (<g><line x1={L} x2={R} y1={y(p)} y2={y(p)} class="grid" /><text x={L - 8} y={y(p) + 4} class="m" text-anchor="end">{Math.round(p * 100)}%</text></g>))}
      {N.map((n) => (<text x={x(n)} y={B + 20} class="m" text-anchor="middle">{n}</text>))}
      <text x={(L + R) / 2} y={B + 42} class="m" text-anchor="middle"><tspan data-lang-en>factors tried (all of them pure noise)</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>số factor đã thử (toàn bộ là nhiễu)</tspan></text>
      <path d={path(P2)} class="l2" />
      <path d={path(P3)} class="l3" />
      {N.map((n, i) => (<g><circle cx={x(n)} cy={y(P2[i])} r="3.5" class="d2" /><circle cx={x(n)} cy={y(P3[i])} r="3.5" class="d3" /></g>))}
      <text x={x(5) - 10} y={y(0.208) - 14} class="n red" text-anchor="end"><tspan data-lang-en>bar t &gt; 2</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>ngưỡng t &gt; 2</tspan></text>
      <text x={x(100) + 12} y={y(0.237) + 22} class="n"><tspan data-lang-en>bar t &gt; 3: still 24% at N = 100</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>ngưỡng t &gt; 3: vẫn 24% khi N = 100</tspan></text>
      <text x={x(400) - 6} y={y(0.661) - 12} class="n" text-anchor="end">66%</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Computed, not observed. Each factor is noise with a mean of zero; the bar is a two-sided t-statistic. The chance that one factor passes is 4.6% at t &gt; 2 and 0.27% at t &gt; 3.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Số tính ra, không phải quan sát. Mỗi factor là nhiễu có trung bình bằng 0; ngưỡng là t-statistic hai phía. Xác suất một factor vượt ngưỡng là 4,6% với t &gt; 2 và 0,27% với t &gt; 3.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .p06f { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .p06f-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .p06f svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .p06f text { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .p06f .h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p06f .m { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .p06f .n { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p06f .n.red { fill: var(--red); }
  .p06f .grid { stroke: var(--border); }
  .p06f .l2 { fill: none; stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 2.2; }
  .p06f .l3 { fill: none; stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 2.2; }
  .p06f .d2 { fill: var(--red); }
  .p06f .d3 { fill: var(--text); }
  .p06f figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
